            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sheila C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My daughter loves fresh pasta when she gets home from school. To speed things up...I cook the whole box. Place single servings in small zip-top bags and pop them in the freezer. All she has to do is dump a bag onto a plate...microwave it for 1 minute then top it with some sauce and microwave it for 1 more minute."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Roxanne J.R."
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this idea! It is especially good for those busy days/evenings. When I first tried this recipe I was having a busy day so I made this in the morning and then re-boiled half of it in the evening for a quick dinner. I froze the other half of the pasta in an airtight bag - which I had today and it was so convenient since I was in a hurry. Definitely worth five stars. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-08T14:23:43.483Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Terry"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm trying this as I prepare for 8 weeks of travel in our camper through Canada and Alaska. I will be freezing it and pulling out pasta as needed / desired. And I have two daughtes-in-law expecting in Oct-Nov so a great way to help them out if it works.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-21T18:54:18.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KINEM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I agree, may as well cook fresh. Someone told me to just put your frozen or cold pasta in a colendar, boil water in the kettle and pour it over. Works like a charm and it steaming hot.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-16T16:15:24.010Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RENWIC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been to a pasta bar where they used this same technique. That way the pasta was ready for a large group when they wanted it. They used a canister with holes, you chose the pasta type, they added a serving to the canister, dunked it into the boiling pots for 1-2 minutes and your pasta was ready for your choice of sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-04T16:36:57.593Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MARY DOMAZ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great way to save time when you need a quick meal. However, you can use a lot less oil than the recipe calls for. Also, I freeze the pasta for future meals. It comes out great!!!",
            "datePublished": "2003-03-25T07:54:59.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
